* * *\nL18: \nL19:   * 【11†history】\nL20:   * 【12†statistics】\nL21: \nL22: 【8†Lemma 5.28.8.】 Let $X$ be a Noetherian topological space. Any finite partition of $X$ can be refined by a finite good stratification.\nL23: Proof. Let $X = \\coprod X_ i$ be a finite partition of $X$. Let $Z$ be an irreducible component of $X$. Since $X = \\bigcup \\overline{X_ i}$ with finite index set, there is an $i$ such that $Z \\subset \\overline{X_ i}$. Since $X_ i$ is locally closed this implies that $Z \\cap X_ i$ contains an open of $Z$. Thus $Z \\cap X_ i$ contains an open $U$ of $X$ (Lemma 【13†5.9.2】).\nL24: Write $X_ i = U \\amalg X_ i^1 \\amalg X_ i^2$ with $X_ i^1 = (X_ i \\setminus U) \\cap \\overline{U}$ and $X_ i^2 = (X_ i \\setminus U) \\cap \\overline{U}^ c$. For $i' \\not= i$ we set $X_{i'}^1 = X_{i'} \\cap \\overline{U}$ and $X_{i'}^2 = X_{i'} \\cap \\overline{U}^ c$. Then\nL25: \\[ X \\setminus U = \\coprod X^ k_ l \\]\nL26: \nL27: is a partition such that $\\overline{U} \\setminus U = \\bigcup X_ l^1$. Note that $X \\setminus U$ is closed and strictly smaller than $X$. By Noetherian induction we can refine this partition by a finite good stratification $X \\setminus U = \\coprod _{\\alpha \\in A} T_\\alpha $. Then $X = U \\amalg \\coprod _{\\alpha \\in A} T_\\alpha $ is a finite good stratification of $X$ refining the partition we started with. $\\square$\nL28: \nL29: * * *\nL30: ## Comments (0)\nL31: \nL32: There are also:\nL33: \nL34:   * 2 comment(s) on Section 【14†5.28】: Partitions and stratifications\nL35: \nL36: * * *\nL37: ## Post a comment\nL38: \nL39: Your email address will not be published. Required fields are marked.\nL40: \nL41: In your comment you can use 【15†Markdown】 and LaTeX style mathematics (enclose it like `$\\pi$`). A preview option is available if you wish to see how it works out (just click on the eye in the toolbar).\nL42: \nL43: Unfortunately JavaScript is disabled in your browser, so the comment preview function will not work.\nL44: \nL45: